BT /F2 13 Tf 48 639.1999999999996 Td (7. Destructive Data Reset Architecture \(POST /api/dashboard/reset-data\)) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.5 Tf 48 607.6999999999996 Td (7.1 Objective & Safety Guarantees) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.35 Tf 48 592.6999999999996 Td (In real data engineering operations, operators require the ability to purge staging or test data to reset the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.35 Tf 48 581.6999999999996 Td (platform state without administrative intervention or dropping the database schema. The destructive data reset was) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.35 Tf 48 570.6999999999996 Td (engineered to meet the following non-negotiable safety criteria:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 58 559.6999999999996 Td (1. Zero Schema Modification: Does not drop tables, alter column definitions, or delete the SQLite database file) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 58 548.9999999999995 Td (\(edvexa_data.db\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 58 538.2999999999995 Td (2. Atomic Transactional Rollback: All deletions execute inside an explicit SQLAlchemy transaction. If any stage) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 58 527.5999999999995 Td (fails, the entire transaction rolls back via db.rollback\(\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 58 516.8999999999994 Td (3. Concurrency Locking: Employs an in-process re-entrant lock \(threading.Lock\(\)\) preventing concurrent upload or) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 58 506.1999999999994 Td (reset requests from causing race conditions or deadlocks.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 58 495.49999999999943 Td (4. Physical File Unlinking: Cleans up stored uploaded CSV files in settings.UPLOADS_DIR using path-traversal) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 58 484.79999999999944 Td (safeguards \(file_path.resolve\(\).is_relative_to\(upload_dir_resolved\)\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 58 474.09999999999945 Td (5. Separation from Preference Resets: POST /api/dashboard/reset-preferences resets client UI preferences \(theme,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 58 463.39999999999947 Td (filters\), whereas POST /api/dashboard/reset-data performs the permanent data purge.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.5 Tf 48 443.1999999999995 Td (7.2 Foreign-Key Safe Deletion Order) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.35 Tf 48 428.1999999999995 Td (SQLite enforces foreign key constraints. The deletion sequence must cascade from dependent child tables to parent) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.35 Tf 48 417.1999999999995 Td (entities:) Tj ET
